    "result_text": "Done. Tests are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`), and the AUDIT line still fires correctly on create.\n\n## What I changed\n\nI agree with the finding and moved the audit emission to the right unit:\n\n- **Reverted** `OwnerRestControllerV1` back to a plain delegating handler (removed the logger and the log line).\n- **Moved the `AUDIT` logger and emission into `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`**, where `registrationDate` and `customerCode` are actually computed. This makes it the single choke point that covers every create caller (V2, importers, batch jobs), not just the V1 controller.\n\nKey correctness detail the finding called out: `saveOwner` is shared with `updateOwner`, so the emission must stay create-only. I captured `boolean creating = owner.isNew()` **before** `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (since the save assigns the id and flips `isNew()` to false), then emit **after** the save gated on `creating` \u2014 so `owner.getId()` is populated in the log line, and updates don't emit.\n\nThe message format is unchanged, so all acceptance behaviour is intact and the log still carries the id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.",
